1
00:01:30,006 --> 00:01:48,306
So, what's going on, Shinwa?

2
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:50,426
I don't know anything more than you do.

3
00:01:53,866 --> 00:01:55,086
Where are the choppers?

4
00:01:55,626 --> 00:01:58,066
Gurren said they would be here waiting to evacuate us.

5
00:01:58,066 --> 00:02:03,646
We're not safe here. The vampires will be close behind. We can't just stand around.

6
00:02:04,326 --> 00:02:09,346
Major General, these directives were in the flight control room. I think they're for us.

7
00:02:18,686 --> 00:02:20,646
Well, what does it say?

8
00:02:23,886 --> 00:02:26,766
To stand by and wait for new orders.

9
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:28,006
Stand by?

10
00:02:28,266 --> 00:02:30,766
This is all your fault, you spoiled little bitch!

11
00:02:35,766 --> 00:02:40,386
Yayoi, Kageyama, they're both dead because you betrayed us and protected that vampire!

12
00:02:41,006 --> 00:02:44,526
It's not fair that you're still alive! Maybe you should join them!

13
00:02:45,166 --> 00:02:46,366
It's all your fault!

14
00:02:47,106 --> 00:02:48,806
You got my friends killed!

15
00:02:48,806 --> 00:02:52,306
I'm sorry.

16
00:02:53,566 --> 00:02:55,226
I'm not forgiving you that easily!

17
00:02:55,646 --> 00:02:57,146
Don't pay for what you did!

18
00:02:58,886 --> 00:03:00,606
Stop! It's fine, you guys!

19
00:03:00,606 --> 00:03:04,226
I don't want your apology!

20
00:03:04,226 --> 00:03:08,746
Save your breath! It won't bring my friends back!

21
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:11,246
They're bleeding in the streets!

22
00:03:12,166 --> 00:03:13,106
You killed them!

23
00:03:17,446 --> 00:03:19,706
Rika, pull yourself together.

24
00:03:20,786 --> 00:03:22,206
Killing her isn't going to help.

25
00:03:22,666 --> 00:03:23,606
But, Makoto...

26
00:03:23,606 --> 00:03:26,566
I'm not saying that I'm going to forgive her or her team.

27
00:03:29,226 --> 00:03:31,926
I'm your leader, so her blood should be on my hands.

28
00:03:34,366 --> 00:03:36,986
Sorry, but that's not your decision to make.

29
00:03:37,886 --> 00:03:39,546
Then you're gonna punish them, right?

30
00:03:40,226 --> 00:03:44,186
They sided with a vampire on the battlefield, which led to our troops being ambushed.

31
00:03:44,186 --> 00:03:49,066
Like I said, you don't get to decide what happens to them.

32
00:03:49,186 --> 00:03:49,686
Fine, then.

33
00:03:49,986 --> 00:03:52,506
Prove you've got what it takes to lead us and punish them!

34
00:03:54,206 --> 00:03:56,946
This entire mission has turned into a giant shitstorm.

35
00:03:57,406 --> 00:03:58,166
Just look at us!

36
00:03:58,406 --> 00:04:00,646
We've lost several of our comrades and our commander.

37
00:04:00,826 --> 00:04:02,966
But we kept moving forward, following orders!

38
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,646
And look how well that's working out.

39
00:04:09,226 --> 00:04:11,806
You want us to forgive these traitors and stand by?

40
00:04:11,806 --> 00:04:15,446
Are we supposed to just lie down and die out here?

41
00:04:19,946 --> 00:04:21,206
Escape in the chopper.

42
00:04:21,866 --> 00:04:25,006
Then lead the vampires to a trap waiting for them in Shinjuku.

43
00:04:26,166 --> 00:04:28,066
That's what our final mission was.

44
00:04:29,006 --> 00:04:31,986
Only thing is, Gurren's not the one who planned this.

45
00:04:32,546 --> 00:04:33,286
Then who did?

46
00:04:36,606 --> 00:04:38,726
Lieutenant General Kuruto Hiragi.

47
00:04:41,806 --> 00:04:45,206
Of course, I'm sick of the Hiragis.

48
00:04:45,926 --> 00:04:49,186
The selfish orders they give out only serve to give them more power.

49
00:04:49,646 --> 00:04:51,426
Well, I refuse to follow it anymore!

50
00:04:53,706 --> 00:04:54,826
Just calm down.

51
00:04:55,626 --> 00:04:57,686
Freaking out isn't going to help us figure out what...

52
00:04:57,686 --> 00:04:59,686
Don't you dare tell me to calm down!

53
00:04:59,686 --> 00:05:07,626
We're abandoning this mission.

54
00:05:07,906 --> 00:05:09,946
I'm going back to rescue the lieutenant colonel.

55
00:05:12,906 --> 00:05:14,666
If he's going back, so am I.

56
00:05:14,946 --> 00:05:15,326
You coming?

57
00:05:15,766 --> 00:05:19,046
If this wasn't Gurren's mission, I don't see any reason to finish it, right?

58
00:05:19,046 --> 00:05:24,366
Goshi, Mito, Shinya, goodbye.

59
00:05:25,506 --> 00:05:26,106
Shigure!

60
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:27,306
Sayuri!

61
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:28,746
Think about this!

62
00:05:30,146 --> 00:05:31,766
This is starting to get ugly.

63
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:33,246
What should we do?

64
00:05:33,246 --> 00:05:50,506
Hold on, Narumi.

65
00:05:50,706 --> 00:05:52,346
I know I'm disobeying orders.

66
00:05:52,746 --> 00:05:54,786
Go ahead and court-martial me for all I care.

67
00:05:55,346 --> 00:05:58,046
Ah, just shut up for a second and listen to me.

68
00:05:58,746 --> 00:06:01,246
I'm trying to tell you that we're aborting this mission together.

69
00:06:01,906 --> 00:06:02,426
What?

70
00:06:04,286 --> 00:06:05,206
Let's do it.

71
00:06:05,326 --> 00:06:07,026
We'll ignore the orders from High Command.

72
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,586
From now on, the Demon Company has one goal.

73
00:06:09,846 --> 00:06:12,166
The rescue of Lieutenant Colonel Gurren Ichinose.

74
00:06:14,006 --> 00:06:14,526
Seriously?

75
00:06:22,306 --> 00:06:24,026
You heard him. Let's go.

76
00:06:24,506 --> 00:06:26,886
We're not going to abandon our friend when he needs our help.

77
00:06:31,246 --> 00:06:50,366
It looks like we missed an impressive battle here.

78
00:06:50,366 --> 00:07:03,746
Start talking, maggot.

79
00:07:05,206 --> 00:07:06,526
What were your plans?

80
00:07:08,126 --> 00:07:10,026
You'll have to hit me harder than that.

81
00:07:12,526 --> 00:07:15,366
Queen Cruel specifically ordered us not to kill him.

82
00:07:15,366 --> 00:07:18,746
Soon he'll be begging to be put out of his misery.

83
00:07:20,546 --> 00:07:21,226
All right.

84
00:07:21,426 --> 00:07:22,946
This is starting to get a little painful.

85
00:07:23,546 --> 00:07:26,146
Time to leak some false intel and buy myself a break.

86
00:07:26,766 --> 00:07:27,486
Let's see.

87
00:07:28,026 --> 00:07:30,606
I've got to get these bastards to Shinjuku somehow.

88
00:07:31,286 --> 00:07:33,366
They've probably beat me enough to believe I've broken.

89
00:07:33,366 --> 00:07:38,326
It's not nap time for the livestock yet.

90
00:07:40,226 --> 00:07:42,186
What a pleasure to see you, Crowley.

91
00:07:44,706 --> 00:07:46,046
It's been too long.

92
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:48,226
Five nobles were killed today.

93
00:07:48,486 --> 00:07:50,166
The humans knew their locations.

94
00:07:50,686 --> 00:07:53,486
I'm positive that you had something to do with this, Lord Farad.

95
00:07:53,486 --> 00:07:54,846
I'm hurt.

96
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,006
There's nothing worse than selling out your friends, right?

97
00:07:58,146 --> 00:07:59,126
That's despicable.

98
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:00,546
Yeah.

99
00:08:01,026 --> 00:08:01,546
True.

100
00:08:01,806 --> 00:08:03,106
But that's not what concerns me.

101
00:08:04,566 --> 00:08:09,206
What bothers me is that you gave the humans my location, too.

102
00:08:09,606 --> 00:08:12,526
And here I was under the impression that I was your friend.

103
00:08:13,206 --> 00:08:15,126
But surely you enjoyed the fight.

104
00:08:15,126 --> 00:08:20,126
Well, yeah, I guess it was a pretty good time.

105
00:08:20,726 --> 00:08:22,346
Then you should be thanking me instead.

106
00:08:23,206 --> 00:08:25,746
Besides, everyone knows that we're friends, Crowley.

107
00:08:25,926 --> 00:08:28,526
No one will suspect I leaked info if you were attacked.

108
00:08:29,046 --> 00:08:29,686
I see.

109
00:08:29,806 --> 00:08:31,666
So you were the one behind this.

110
00:08:32,306 --> 00:08:33,646
You're only half right.

111
00:08:33,646 --> 00:08:37,086
There's actually another puppeteer pulling the strings along with me.

112
00:08:37,486 --> 00:08:37,666
Oh?

113
00:08:38,086 --> 00:08:38,766
Who is it?

114
00:08:44,246 --> 00:08:44,806
Him.

115
00:08:45,126 --> 00:08:52,206
You must have some kind of death wish, human.

116
00:09:01,806 --> 00:09:03,246
How dare you!

117
00:09:09,726 --> 00:09:11,366
Okay, I've had enough of this.

118
00:09:12,006 --> 00:09:13,446
It's Shinjuku.

119
00:09:13,446 --> 00:09:16,266
You're dead, filthy human!

120
00:09:16,446 --> 00:09:17,446
Okay, stop it.

121
00:09:17,686 --> 00:09:18,746
He's saying something.

122
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:19,626
I don't care!

123
00:09:20,846 --> 00:09:23,066
The lieutenant colonel is a half-demon.

124
00:09:23,326 --> 00:09:23,666
Hmm?

125
00:09:23,866 --> 00:09:24,786
A half-demon?

126
00:09:25,026 --> 00:09:27,366
Although he's actually close to becoming complete.

127
00:09:28,246 --> 00:09:32,406
Every day he struggles to keep two personalities under control inside his body.

128
00:09:32,406 --> 00:09:40,486
One is an idealist who wants nothing more than to protect his troops and his friends from harm.

129
00:09:40,486 --> 00:09:50,766
Come on now.

130
00:09:50,766 --> 00:09:50,826
Come on now.

131
00:09:51,366 --> 00:09:53,426
You've had more than enough of this, my darling.

132
00:09:55,166 --> 00:09:57,226
Relax and let me take over a while.

133
00:09:58,706 --> 00:09:59,666
Get lost.

134
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:02,666
My poor little soldier.

135
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:06,346
You don't even have the strength to push me away right now.

136
00:10:06,346 --> 00:10:17,086
But the other personality isn't so nice.

137
00:10:17,446 --> 00:10:19,026
It's his dead ex-girlfriend.

138
00:10:19,366 --> 00:10:21,906
A perfectionist who's been turned into a demon.

139
00:10:21,906 --> 00:10:24,846
Look, the monster is coming out.

140
00:10:26,226 --> 00:10:27,606
You're dead, human!

141
00:10:27,866 --> 00:10:28,346
Die!

142
00:10:29,386 --> 00:10:33,626
Enjoy your last few seconds alive, bloodsucker.

143
00:10:34,626 --> 00:10:35,026
What?

144
00:10:35,186 --> 00:10:36,806
How dare you speak to me like that?

145
00:10:36,806 --> 00:10:48,846
Give it here, my hero.

146
00:10:55,846 --> 00:10:57,026
Oh, I see.

147
00:10:57,586 --> 00:10:59,066
You're the one in control.

148
00:11:06,806 --> 00:11:07,806
Help her!

149
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:08,646
Kill him!

150
00:11:08,766 --> 00:11:09,706
Stay where you are!

151
00:11:11,406 --> 00:11:14,446
Now then, you're Mahiru Hiragi's messenger.

152
00:11:15,106 --> 00:11:16,166
So where is she?

153
00:11:18,026 --> 00:11:19,086
Mahiru is dead.

154
00:11:19,686 --> 00:11:22,566
My deal was with her before the world ended.

155
00:11:22,746 --> 00:11:25,546
If she's dead, then there's no reason for me to keep you alive.

156
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:28,306
Our agreement is null and void in this circumstance.

157
00:11:28,766 --> 00:11:30,106
Then go ahead and kill me.

158
00:11:31,126 --> 00:11:32,146
Oh, that's right.

159
00:11:32,246 --> 00:11:33,246
You can't do it.

160
00:11:33,246 --> 00:11:38,146
You've already betrayed your kind and need the humans to bail your sorry ass out, right?

161
00:11:38,986 --> 00:11:40,146
The serif of the end?

162
00:11:40,566 --> 00:11:43,326
The experiment has to succeed today or you're totally screwed.

163
00:11:48,026 --> 00:11:49,046
Smart thinking.

164
00:11:49,686 --> 00:11:52,666
Make them believe you're still on their side, not a complete traitor.

165
00:11:53,526 --> 00:11:55,086
They'll be testing it at the airport.

166
00:11:57,386 --> 00:11:58,286
Attention, men!

167
00:11:58,286 --> 00:12:00,946
The humans are reassembling at the Nagaya Airport.

168
00:12:01,386 --> 00:12:02,686
Old units, move out!

169
00:12:02,686 --> 00:12:03,546
Ma'am!

170
00:12:12,546 --> 00:12:14,926
So, what's going to happen now, Ferret?

171
00:12:15,126 --> 00:12:16,086
What's the endgame?

172
00:12:17,766 --> 00:12:20,046
The transformation of the world.

173
00:12:27,086 --> 00:12:27,806
Vampires?

174
00:12:28,026 --> 00:12:28,386
Yuichi!

175
00:12:28,726 --> 00:12:29,086
Right.

176
00:12:30,866 --> 00:12:31,906
Don't fire!

177
00:12:31,906 --> 00:12:32,346
They're...

178
00:12:32,346 --> 00:12:34,266
They're ours.

179
00:12:35,346 --> 00:12:37,126
Those are Demon Army aircraft.

180
00:12:37,126 --> 00:12:37,166
Those are Demon Army aircraft.

181
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:51,486
Big sister!

182
00:12:51,486 --> 00:12:51,566
Big sister!

183
00:12:51,566 --> 00:12:52,246
Serpent,ansa...

184
00:12:52,246 --> 00:12:52,986
...

185
00:12:52,986 --> 00:12:57,086
Hey!

186
00:13:08,086 --> 00:13:09,506
He's the one who tortured us.

187
00:13:09,506 --> 00:13:10,526
Good нуж aim.

188
00:13:12,126 --> 00:13:13,486
Kurato.

189
00:13:13,906 --> 00:13:14,726
Shiragi.

190
00:13:14,726 --> 00:13:33,306
Attention! I'm Lieutenant General Kureto Hiragi.

191
00:13:33,846 --> 00:13:36,746
As you likely know, my family controls the Demon Army.

192
00:13:41,726 --> 00:13:43,486
I've heard stories about him.

193
00:13:43,486 --> 00:13:44,466
Me too.

194
00:13:44,726 --> 00:13:47,926
Rumor has it he's next in line as head of the Hiragis and the army.

195
00:13:49,606 --> 00:13:53,366
Because of your efforts, we're looking at total victory over the Vampires.

196
00:13:53,726 --> 00:13:56,986
The sacrifices of the Moon Demon Company will not have been in vain.

197
00:13:57,346 --> 00:13:59,126
You have ensured humanity's survival.

198
00:13:59,866 --> 00:14:01,446
My team will take over from here.

199
00:14:02,086 --> 00:14:03,626
Enjoy some much-deserved downtime.

200
00:14:04,126 --> 00:14:05,006
Disarm and relax.

201
00:14:07,686 --> 00:14:10,186
Does that mean our mission's over?

202
00:14:10,886 --> 00:14:11,926
Sounds like it.

203
00:14:11,926 --> 00:14:14,206
Makoto, did you hear that?

204
00:14:14,206 --> 00:14:20,286
Everyone, stay at attention and ready to fight just in case.

205
00:14:20,286 --> 00:14:24,266
Total victory, huh?

206
00:14:24,766 --> 00:14:27,126
Vampire nobles are headed this way as we speak.

207
00:14:27,826 --> 00:14:29,846
So how do you plan to defeat them, brother?

208
00:14:31,206 --> 00:14:31,646
Brutally.

209
00:14:32,046 --> 00:14:33,886
We lost a lot of comrades here.

210
00:14:33,966 --> 00:14:35,886
Don't we deserve to know what your plan is?

211
00:14:35,886 --> 00:14:36,466
Where is Gurren?

212
00:14:37,806 --> 00:14:39,806
He was captured by the Vampires.

213
00:14:40,206 --> 00:14:40,406
Huh?

214
00:14:40,646 --> 00:14:41,906
Please tell me you're joking.

215
00:14:43,866 --> 00:14:44,526
Damn it.

216
00:14:45,066 --> 00:14:45,666
That fool.

217
00:14:47,106 --> 00:14:48,566
Is he turning on me as well?

218
00:14:49,086 --> 00:14:51,306
Which personality was in control when they took him?

219
00:14:51,866 --> 00:14:52,186
Huh?

220
00:14:52,186 --> 00:14:53,526
Come on.

221
00:14:53,686 --> 00:14:54,966
You haven't figured it out yet.

222
00:14:55,646 --> 00:14:56,566
Figured what out?

223
00:14:56,666 --> 00:15:00,546
Well, he did always try to keep his comrades protected and in the dark.

224
00:15:00,746 --> 00:15:03,686
But I'm surprised you didn't catch on since you were so close.

225
00:15:03,786 --> 00:15:04,826
What are you talking about?

226
00:15:05,066 --> 00:15:05,906
Gurren's been taken!

227
00:15:06,006 --> 00:15:06,646
That's enough.

228
00:15:07,566 --> 00:15:08,786
Your part in this is over.

229
00:15:09,346 --> 00:15:09,686
Aoi.

230
00:15:10,106 --> 00:15:10,526
Do it.

231
00:15:10,526 --> 00:15:12,286
Yes, sir.

232
00:15:31,446 --> 00:15:32,326
Wait, Kurito.

233
00:15:32,706 --> 00:15:34,326
What in the hell is going on?

234
00:15:34,466 --> 00:15:36,586
I told you, your role in this is complete.

235
00:15:37,006 --> 00:15:38,446
What are you planning to do?

236
00:15:40,526 --> 00:15:43,986
Hey!

237
00:15:45,906 --> 00:15:47,406
Stand down, right now.

238
00:15:47,726 --> 00:15:49,946
I don't know who you are, but I told you to relax.

239
00:15:50,306 --> 00:15:51,366
Follow my orders.

240
00:15:51,826 --> 00:15:52,786
Screw your orders!

241
00:15:53,186 --> 00:15:53,566
What?

242
00:15:53,646 --> 00:15:55,326
You think you can show up here and...

243
00:15:55,326 --> 00:15:56,666
Calm down.

244
00:15:57,086 --> 00:15:58,406
Makoto, ease up.

245
00:16:06,086 --> 00:16:06,906
Not good.

246
00:16:07,246 --> 00:16:08,346
What have you done, brother?

247
00:16:10,526 --> 00:16:32,066
Don't bother.

248
00:16:32,066 --> 00:16:34,426
You can't hope to protect him.

249
00:16:35,026 --> 00:16:38,786
We completed an impossible suicide mission behind enemy lines.

250
00:16:39,226 --> 00:16:41,426
We did what you asked of us, so just let us go.

251
00:16:42,326 --> 00:16:44,926
And overlook this soldier's rebellious attitude?

252
00:16:47,846 --> 00:16:48,406
Alright.

253
00:16:48,826 --> 00:16:49,706
I'll let it slide.

254
00:16:50,246 --> 00:16:51,506
Don't want to spoil the fun.

255
00:16:51,506 --> 00:16:57,046
Besides, he's going to die soon anyway.

256
00:16:57,466 --> 00:16:57,946
Shit.

257
00:16:58,506 --> 00:16:58,926
Begin!

258
00:16:58,926 --> 00:16:58,966
Begin!

259
00:17:15,966 --> 00:17:17,306
Get push him!

260
00:17:17,306 --> 00:17:20,106
Arison Kin.

261
00:17:24,306 --> 00:17:29,566
Arison Kin.

262
00:17:33,626 --> 00:17:34,786
Arise.

263
00:17:34,786 --> 00:17:36,206
Arison Kin.

264
00:17:37,066 --> 00:17:37,746
No.

265
00:17:37,846 --> 00:17:38,326
Akoto.

266
00:17:38,686 --> 00:17:39,226
Run!

267
00:17:39,486 --> 00:17:40,746
Arison Kin.

268
00:17:40,866 --> 00:17:42,546
Right.

269
00:17:42,606 --> 00:17:44,026
Arison Kin!

270
00:17:44,446 --> 00:17:45,446
Arison Kin.

271
00:17:45,446 --> 00:17:57,446
Damn you!

272
